# Idle: battery-9v (9.0 V EMF, 1.7 ohm 1 kHz impedance) feeds the Nano (~26 mA) and LM7805 +
# green LED through 470 ohm (~17 mA), ~43 mA total (within Energizer 522's 50 mA characterized
# continuous load), sagging ~0.07 V to ~8.93 V with no warnings.
# With btn1 held, the 25 ohm load draws ~334 mA (~376 mA total), sagging the battery rail to
# ~8.36 V (0.57 V extra drop) while LM7805 holds 5.00 V and battery-9v warns that the load is
# beyond the 50 mA continuous load Energizer 522 characterizes.
open
step 100ms
expect @led1 lit
expect @bat.pos > 8.85V
expect @bat.pos < 8.98V
expect @reg.OUT > 4.95V
expect @reg.OUT < 5.05V
expect @nano.5V > 4.95V
expect serial contains "bat=8.9"
expect no diagnostics
press @btn1
step 100ms
expect @bat.pos > 8.28V
expect @bat.pos < 8.44V
expect @reg.OUT > 4.95V
expect @reg.OUT < 5.05V
expect @led1 lit
expect serial contains "bat=8.3"
release @btn1
step 100ms
expect @bat.pos > 8.85V
expect diagnostics contains "warning[rating.current]"
expect diagnostics contains "beyond the 50 mA load its sheet characterizes"
